# Private keys, wherever they land.
#
# Keys for this project live in ~/.conduit-keys, outside the repository and
# chmod 600, precisely so this section never has to work. It is here for the
# time somebody generates one in the wrong directory, or copies a file across
# to "check something" and forgets. A key that reaches a public repo is
# compromised the moment it is pushed, and no amount of rewriting history
# afterwards makes it not have been there -- so the cheap defence is to make
# the accident impossible to commit rather than to catch it in review.
*.key
*.seed
*.pem
*.p12
*.keystore
keystore/
.conduit-keys/
**/private-key*
**/privatekey*

# ── TypeScript ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ── OS / Editor ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo


# Internal working notes — process records, not product docs. Kept local.
audit/
packages/app/audit/
.vercel

# Internal error-code reference (not for the repo)
errorcodes.md

# Migration working notes — local planning record, not product docs.
privy-removal.md

# Build-process records, not documentation.
#
# STATUS.md is a gate-by-gate report of how the product was built, with pasted
# shell output; docs/cctp-capability.md is a point-in-time "can Circle do X"
# investigation that ends in a devnet faucet being empty. Both were useful while
# the work was happening and neither is something a new engineer should read to
# understand this codebase. Kept locally, out of the repo.
STATUS.md
docs/cctp-capability.md

# Progress record for the security hardening pass: phase, change, gate output.
# Same reasoning as STATUS.md -- it is how the work went, not what the code is.
whereistopped.md

# Patch files from local review and rebase work.
*.patch

# Working log for the in-flight audit. Local only.
PROGRESS.md
